  "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: two Landscape Identity Implicit Association Tests (LI-IAT) pair the words Self (I, Me, Mine, Myself) and Other (It, Other, Their, Them) with four European vs four Not-European landscape photos and with four Mediterranean vs four Not-Mediterranean photos, in the classic seven-block layout (20, 20, 20+40, 20, 20+40 trials). Then two eight-figure items on how much the self overlaps with Europe and with the Mediterranean, and a 1–5 pleasantness rating of all 16 landscapes. Rebuilt from Fornara, Dentale, Troffa & Piras (2016), Frontiers in Psychology 7: 1259, with the photos of its Figures 1–4 (CC BY 4.0). Analysis: one-sample t-tests of each D score against 0, correlations of D with the matching identity item, pleasantness differences (European minus Not European, Mediterranean minus Not Mediterranean) as controls in a regression.",
